{
  "_": [
    "v0.29.1 D7 — the note GRAPH's five read predicates, pinned as shared vectors.",
    "",
    "Two implementations answer these questions on opposite ends of the sync wire: the server's",
    "SQL (packages/core/src/db/link.rs + db/tag.rs) and the CLI's local inversion of the payload",
    "(apps/cli/src/graph.rs). They ship on different release trains, so this file is the contract.",
    "",
    "MEMBERSHIP is pinned, not sequence. Both sides sort by path (or tag) for presentation, but",
    "the server evaluates ORDER BY under the database collation (en_US.UTF-8 here — a locale",
    "collation, not byte order) and the client cannot reproduce that without shipping a collation",
    "engine. Both consumers therefore compare these as SETS. An order that differs is a",
    "differently-sorted right answer; a set that differs is a wrong one.",
    "",
    "Node ids are SYMBOLIC keys: the server test gets whatever uuids its inserts mint, the client",
    "test synthesizes its own. Each side maps keys to its ids and back.",
    "",
    "Synthetic fixture only — this crate is MIT and ships in the public CLI mirror, so real",
    "workspace paths must never land here."
  ],
